<title>HONG KONG: Shell unit to run stations at HK airport.</title>
<headline>Shell unit to run stations at HK airport.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-05-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hong Kong's Airport Authority said on Wednesday it signed a 15-year agreement with a Royal Dutch Shell Group unit to develop and operate two petrol filling stations at the new Chek Lap Kok airport.</p>
<p>Shell Hong Kong Ltd will operate the two 1,500-square-metre stations round the clock, the authority said in a statement.</p>
<p>The new airport, now under construction, will begin operations next April.</p>
<p>Another Shell unit, Shell Developments (HK), is part of Aviation Fuel Supply Co, a consortium of nine international companies that has a 20-year franchise to build and operate the aviation fuel system at Chek Lap Kok.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong newsroom (852) 2843 6590</p>
